{
  "name": "llm-advanced-det (the developer fields of the server form: timeout and extra JSON parameters, each refusal, then cancelled without saving; gone with the developer mode off)",
  "stopOnError": false,
  "notes": [
    "Code-verified against components/ai/ServerForm.svelte and components/ai/servers.ts (validateServerForm, parsedTimeout, parsedExtraParams).",
    "llm-det opens the form and saves it under stubs with one valid value in each developer field; this book plays the refusals: a timeout under the minimum, over the maximum and not a number, then extra parameters that are not JSON, not an object, and that name a reserved field.",
    "A refused form stays open: ai-server-save validates before any call (ServerForm.svelte save), so no IPC leaves and no stub is needed. The refusal itself is rendered by FormField under an id, not a testid, so the book asserts the form is still there after each save and leaves the wording to Vitest.",
    "ai-server-save is never accepted: the last valid state is cancelled, so no server is saved and the book is re-runnable.",
    "The form is reached on the ADD path, which needs no saved server; the fields are the same on the edit path."
  ],
  "dynamicTestids": [
    "settings-nav-developer"
  ],
